lane: relaxed-queues-builder
why: the design became a menu -- three channels over four buffers --
  and it wants two more entries and a way to order from it.
what:
  MultiFifo: k sub-buffers, a producer bound to one of them, a
    consumer taking from whichever has something. Contention drops
    with the number of producers; global FIFO is given up, and per
    producer FIFO is NOT, because a producer stays on its part.
  BlockFifo: a caller claims a run of positions and works inside it
    privately, so coordination is per block rather than per element.
  Channels.builder: pick a contract, pick a mechanism, get a channel.
the catch, named up front: a relaxed buffer breaks the end mark.
  SentinelChannel's termination rides the FIFO stream and relies on
  nothing following the mark; with k parts a mark in one part is
  reached while other parts still hold elements. Either such buffers
  serve only AbruptChannel, or close must seal EVERY part and the
  channel count them all -- the second keeps drain-on-close and is
  what to build.
  And Buffer's contract must say which order it promises, the way the
  channel laws already split into tiers: global FIFO, or per-producer
  only. A relaxed buffer that quietly passes a global-FIFO test is a
  test that is not testing.
